# Workshop gallery, scenes 4 to 6 of the shotlist v2 of 2026-10-25 (the plan, the story and the outfit rule are in the header of
# 09-galerie-sanctuaire.feature; the second ticket of the series, three scenes each).
#
# 4 workshop-4-chess (REWRITTEN 2026-11-06 after the director pass: the 23 Oct capture showed a Yorkshire at about 12 px in a 268 px
#   thumbnail, three tan coats alike, Nelim in profile with her face hidden). cloister, 15:00, clear, zoom 2.5 on (174, 128) (5 cells
#   tall, x 169.6 to 178.4, about 30 px a cell at 268 px wide: a Yorkshire is about 17 px side view), +45 ticks then +15. TIGHT shot.
#   Foreground: the plank strip z 126 to 128; background: the fence and the columns at z 129; light under the roof plus the torches.
#   Gesture: Nelim plays chess (JobDef Play_Chess forced on the ChessTable at (172, 126)), first stood at (172, 127) facing South so
#   she sits facing the camera; no hat (roofed), denim shirt, canon Highpony, a smirk and a squint (she is about to win; fallback
#   smile). Instant: her hand is over the board as the third dog trots in (run the job, 30 ticks, start Brume's walk, 15 more ticks).
#   Yorkshire terriers (Core), coats picked to differ: Tweed -1 original black and tan lies down at (174, 127); Brume 0 steel blue
#   walks (forced) from (178, 128) to (175, 127), still mid-step; Brioche 1 sand stands at (176, 127) facing South: the one that faces
#   the camera. Coat 2 (oatmeal, about the original at that size) is not drawn. Decor: the existing ChessTable, KneelPillow and the
#   TorchLamps (170, 126) and (176, 126) (cells from SANCTUAIRE-CASES.md, unchecked in game), Plant_Daylily at (170, 128) and
#   (177, 127); the placed bonsai and the two extra torches are dropped (clutter in a tight frame). No fallback pose: if the job
#   fails the scene is replaced. Fallback for contrast: Brioche coat 0 and Brume coat 1. Estimate 4.5 (-0.5: sand on planks is weak).
#   Subtitle: "A game of chess, watched from below."
#
# 5 workshop-5-evening-training. enclosure-south, 18:00, zoom 4.5 on (158, 211), +45 ticks. Gesture: Nelim, hat on, trains a husky
#   at the gate (JobDef Train forced on the husky "coat-2", she stands beside it, turned to it); instant: she has just given the
#   command, the husky answers. Huskies (Core, coats 0 ice blue, -1 original, 1 coffee, 2 oatmeal): one lies down tired, two follow
#   her within 3 cells, the trained one is the one facing the camera. Decor: Plant_YellowTallGrass at (156, 209) and (162, 212)
#   (placed in e276), the fence and the laying boxes of the pen; painted zones hidden; no torch (the gate cell holds a Fence).
#   Low sun at 18:00. If Train does not start (no training left to give), refile with a Hay haul to (158, 211). Estimate 4.
#   Subtitle: "Evening training, and four huskies at the gate."
#
# 6 workshop-6-fireside. fire-pit, 20:00, zoom 5 on (181, 115), +60 ticks. CLOSING image. Gesture: Nelim, now in the navy Duster over
#   the denim shirt, no hat, plays the harp by the fire (plays the instrument "Harp"; the harp of the ritual hall is hidden first so
#   the step finds ours). Instant: the first notes, the corgis gather. Corgis of Vanilla Animals Expanded (AEXP_Corgi, coats -1,
#   0 taupe, 1 champagne, 2 slate): the original faces the camera at (182, 113), one walks towards the fire from (177, 116), one stands
#   at (183, 114) facing west, one lies down asleep at (179, 113); the white cat of scene 1 (coat -1) sleeps at (179, 117): the
#   evening gathers the day. Decor: Harp at (183, 116), PlantPot_Bonsai (185, 117), lit TorchLamp at (177, 114), (184, 114),
#   (181, 118) (the old (185, 114) holds a Fence). Estimate 4. Subtitle: "By the fire, the corgis keep their own colours."
#
# SHOTS 7 TO 11, WRITTEN 2026-11-06 (rule 5: every animal the mod patches is in a shot; 35 of 41 had none). Director's decision
# (Virginie, 2026-11-06, "c'est toi la réalisatrice"): 11 images in all. Director pass of an Opus sub-agent kept for the cells, the
# coats and the group sizes (at most 9 animals a frame, 6 for the cats), and a research pass over the NPT steps and the NSB
# catalogues kept for the ideas. Plan only: scenarios not written, no ticket. Each shows ONE coat per breed, picked to differ from its
# neighbours; the other coats of the breed are declared not drawn (a group shot cannot tell them apart at 268 px; the 08-revue
# captures show every coat). Nelim: the day's outfit (denim shirt, canon hair), smile, the straw hat only in open sun. Cells marked
# (unchk) are not checked in game, and SANCTUAIRE-CASES.md is dated 2026-10-06. Thumbnail px = 150.75 / (2 x zoom) a cell.
# 7 workshop-7-cats-terrace. terrace x 193-200 z 118-124, 13:00, clear, zoom 4 on (197, 121) (8 cells tall, 18.8 px a cell), +45 ticks.
#   Siesta. Nelim, no hat, Roo_HD_Hair_Highpony, smile, forced haul of 10 Cloth (a blanket) from (193, 120) to (199, 120), mid-stride
#   near (196, 120) as the cats wake. Six cats, one coat each: Core Cat coat 2 peach walks (193, 121) to (197, 121); akaNEKO_Persian 3
#   chocolate lies (194, 124); akaNEKO_Siamese 0 blue walks (200, 121) to (198, 121) to greet her; akaNEKO_Scottish_Fold 2 ashblue
#   lies (197, 123); akaNEKO_Maine_Coon 0 charcoal lies by the Campfire (194, 121) (195, 122); akaNEKO_Russian_Blue 1 coffee stands at
#   (194, 118) facing South: the one facing the camera. Foreground z 118 to 119, Nelim's lane z 120 to 121, sleepers z 122 to 124;
#   light from the Campfire and the TorchLamps (195, 123) and (200, 119) (lit: unchk, else place a TorchLamp at (196, 124)).
#   Risk: the terrace roof (unchk), cats outrunning her (+30 ticks). Estimate 4.5. Subtitle: "One o'clock siesta: six cats take the terrace."
# 8 workshop-8-cats-dining. dining-nook x 169-183 z 104-112 (white rug, table, chairs), 17:00, clear, zoom 4 on its centre (176, 108),
#   +45 ticks. Tea time. Nelim sits on a chair at the table (step "sits on the building"), no hat, smile, a cup of tea beside her; the
#   other six cats (akaNEKO_Scottish_Fold_Long, N_Forest_Cat, J_Bobtail, A_Shorthair, kijitora, AEXP_CatAbyssinian), one coat each
#   chosen on the day from the patch palette to differ from the neighbours, lie on the rug, one on a chair, two walk (forced) towards
#   her; one stands facing South. Cells read from SANCTUAIRE-CASES.md (dining-nook) when the scenario is written. Risk: dark coats
#   on dark rug, then the fallback is the cloister at midday along the colonnade (sunbathing). Estimate 4. Subtitle: "Tea at five:
#   six more cats come to the table."
# 9 workshop-9-dogs-clearing. emerald-clearing x 181-213 z 143-161 (carpet stripped on arrival, unchk), 11:00, clear, zoom 5 on
#   (195, 152) (10 cells tall, 15.1 px a cell, a big dog about 27 px), +60 ticks. Walk. Nelim, straw hat on long loose hair
#   (Roo_Royal_LongHD), smile, forced walk (195, 157) to (195, 148) towards the camera: a front view, mid-stride near (195, 153)
#   as the hounds sprint ahead. Nine Stray Dogs, one coat each: SCGreyhound 1 chocolate sprints (193, 156) to (192, 148); SCBorzoi 0
#   sand sprints (197, 157) to (198, 148); SCAfghanHound 2 mist runs (199, 156) to (201, 149); SCBorderCollie 0 chocolate runs back
#   (191, 150) to (194, 155); SCBullmastiff 2 stone lies (191, 153); SCCaucasianshepherd 0 slate lies (202, 155); SCChowchow 2 ink
#   stands (200, 151) facing West; SCGoldenRetriever 2 sand stands (194, 149) facing South: the one facing the camera; SCBullTerrier 2
#   grey walks at her heel (196, 157) to (196, 149). Decor: none (the torch (196, 145) and the sculpture (186, 146) are out of frame).
#   Risk: dogs stop at their target (+45 ticks). Estimate 4. Subtitle: "Eleven o'clock walk: nine stray dogs, nine coats."
# 10 workshop-10-dogs-horseshoes. calm-zone x 180-220 z 176-198 (cream ground), 16:00, clear, low sun, zoom 4.5 on (200, 186)
#   (9 cells tall, 16.75 px a cell, a small dog about 17 px), +45 ticks. Play. Nelim, straw hat on, smile, at (198, 185) facing East,
#   forced job Play_Horseshoes on a HorseshoesPin placed at (203, 189); the horseshoe has just left her hand and the dogs race it
#   (fallback: forced haul of one WoodLog from (198, 185) to (202, 188), the stick). Nine Stray Dogs, one coat each:
#   StrayDogs_SwedishVallhund 0 slate races (200, 183) to (203, 188); SCWelshCorgi 2 stone races (197, 186) to (202, 190);
#   SCMiniatureDachshund 0 chocolate trails (196, 184) to (200, 187); SCPug 1 ink stands (198, 183) facing South: the one facing the
#   camera; SCSchnauzer 2 coffee walks (204, 182) to (201, 185); SCOldEnglishSheepdog 1 sand stands (201, 183) facing West;
#   SCSaintbernard 1 sand lies (196, 187); SCNewFoundland 1 mist lies (196, 189); StrayDogs_BerneseMountainDog 1 mist lies (204, 184).
#   Flag: the Newfoundland and Bernese coats cannot be told apart at 268 px on near-black sprites, they are there for presence. Risk:
#   the forced job may not choose its stand cell (list the job options first, unchk). Estimate 4. Subtitle: "Horseshoes at four:
#   nine dogs chase every throw."
# 11 workshop-11-dogs-supper. prestige-hall x 193-200 z 106-117 (grey rug, table), 19:00, clear outside, zoom 3.5 on (196, 112)
#   (7 cells tall, 21.5 px a cell, a pug about 19 px), +45 ticks. Supper. Nelim, no hat, no Duster yet (it comes at 20:00), smile,
#   forced haul of 1 MealFine from (194, 113) to (199, 113), mid-stride, the dogs know the way. Five Vanilla Animals Expanded dogs, one
#   coat each: AEXP_GermanShepherd 2 slate walks (193, 114) to (198, 114) round the Brazier (196, 114); AEXP_Beagle 2 stone stands
#   (199, 112) facing West, begging; AEXP_Pug 1 ink lies (194, 111); AEXP_FrenchBulldog 2 chocolate stands (194, 109) facing South:
#   the one facing the camera; AEXP_WelshTerrier 0 mist walks (200, 113) to (200, 109) towards the camera. Decor: two TorchLamps
#   placed and lit at (193, 109) and (200, 110) (the braziers are probably unlit, unchk). Risk: dark indoors at 19:00, the torches.
#   Estimate 4. Subtitle: "Supper at seven: five dogs know the way to the table."
# Day order (reindex at 9.b): 07 (1), 10 (2), 11 (9), 12 (3), 13 (7), 15 (4), 16 (10), 17 (8), 18 (5), 19 (11), 20 (6).
# Ideas kept for later, not written (research pass): the barn east extension for a twelve-cat nap room, a bridge parade on the
# river-bridge, a rain day, a feeding scene with Ingest and Kibble, kittens at life stage 0, one dyed collar per dog, a film-ticks
# run to pick the best mid-stride frame; steps to ask NPT for (arc placement, sitting pose, advance until distance, a camera step on
# several named animals).
#
# Interface windows: none planned (an info card of a breed would be taken on window-backdrop-for-height and cropped, no subtitle).
